WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.460
Welcome to Looper.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.620
I'm Brian Rubin.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.640
Today, we are talking all about the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:22.270
Before 2014, if I told you that one of the
biggest superhero franchises ever would feature

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.570
a talking tree and his raccoon buddy, you'd
probably have called me a stinking liar.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:32.800
And yet, Guardians of the Galaxy is arguably
one of the most popular Marvel movies ever.

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.900
Now I'm joined by Tom and Nina to try and
figure out the answer to this question: Who

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:42.339
are the weirdest characters that could actually
show up in the MCU?

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:46.880
Nina, who are the weirdest characters that
could actually show up in MCU?

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.460
This was fun to look up, I found some weird
stuff.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:56.809
I don't know how likely these are to show
up, but I would not be upset if they did.

00:00:56.809 --> 00:01:02.199
I really liked learning about Thor's sister,
I believe it's pronounced Laussa, who just

00:01:02.199 --> 00:01:05.710
turns into a fire demon at random times.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:09.750
And that starts when she's a baby, so that
means we could see a baby exploding into a

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.520
fire demon with no provocation.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.990
This is something you want to see?

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.299
Yeah, that would be cool.

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:16.299
I'm into this.

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:17.299
All right.

00:01:17.299 --> 00:01:18.299
Okay.

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:21.630
Look, I didn't know I wanted to see Rocket
Raccoon or Groot, and everyone has a Groot

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.040
Funko Pop in their home.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.820
So, baby fire demon is next.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.820
Yeah.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:27.770
Baby fire demon is the obvious leap.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:32.060
I feel like this guy has come up in the good
old Looper Slack thread, but Armless Tiger

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.299
Man could be interesting.

00:01:34.299 --> 00:01:36.299
Armless Tiger Man?

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:37.640
Who's that?

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.020
Are you guys familiar with Eric Hertz?

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:41.049
No.

00:01:41.049 --> 00:01:42.579
Also known as Armless Tiger Man?

00:01:42.579 --> 00:01:52.369
Yeah, in the 1940s he worked in a lab, and
his arms get caught in a machine, and he loses

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:53.369
them.

00:01:53.369 --> 00:01:54.680
Gets bitten by a tiger.

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.680
Yeah.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.359
And he's super, super strong.

00:01:58.359 --> 00:02:06.420
And he just calls himself Armless Tiger Man
and just runs around wrecking stuff.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.200
I have five questions.

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.880
Exactly five?

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:10.880
Yeah.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.431
I just want to start off, okay, so he doesn't
have any arms?

00:02:13.431 --> 00:02:15.270
No, he does not have any arms.

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.880
And not to disparage anybody, but he's also
very, very strong?

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:19.880
Yes.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:20.880
Okay.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.880
Where does the tiger come in?

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:22.880
If he doesn't skip leg day.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:24.420
Unclear as to where the tiger comes in.

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:29.190
Oh, in all the depictions of him, he has fangs
and very pointy teeth.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:30.190
And he's usually-

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.110
Where did he get those?

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.730
The fangs?

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.210
Yeah.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:41.320
Oh, he got the teeth to use in place of his
arms for more attack power.

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:42.320
Okay.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.320
It's actually going to be six questions.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.500
Who puts the teeth in for him?

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:52.960
I will have to direct you to my forthcoming
book, Armless Tiger Man, A Biography, that

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.310
I'm currently working on.

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:55.350
Reserving it on Amazon.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:59.710
Finally, if you don't mind, I'm sorry to keep
interrupting, but I'm very excited about this

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:00.710
subject.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.710
It's fine.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:05.290
Which hero pulled the short straw on this
one?

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.090
Whose nemesis is Armless Tiger Man?

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.720
Black Panther.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.680
Oh, that's sad.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:12.950
It is.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.800
Because he's another big cat with arms.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.090
Yeah, he does have arms.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.580
So that's an immediate disadvantage.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:25.720
But if, say, Shuri dons the suit, maybe she
has to fight an Armless Tiger Man in doing

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.370
so.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:28.370
I don't see Ryan Coogler-

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:29.370
That doesn't make me feel better.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.370
She's a very smart woman.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.630
She's got a lot going for her.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.740
I don't feel myself.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.930
So your concerned about the Armless Tiger
Man?

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.710
You're worried about his wellbeing?

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:41.020
I'm nothing but concerned about the Armless
Tiger Man.

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:43.750
I'm worried about Daredevil too-

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.940
See, this is working.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.710
I'm drumming up sympathy in this character.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.710
It's already working.

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.640
That's a good point.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.880
And my final one is Ruby Thursday.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.330
Are you guys familiar with her?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:59.800
Nina, did you fall asleep under too many blankets?

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.040
Where are these coming from?

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:06.630
These are straight out of Marvel.com.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:11.930
She is part of like the Headmen or something,
and she has a plastic head like Mr. Potato

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:14.650
Head, where she can move stuff around on it.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:19.160
Sometimes she just turns into an enormous
pair of plastic lips.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.220
And then she fights...?

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.220
Mm-hmm (affirmative).

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.220
Who does she fight?

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.340
Oh, and then she fights, okay.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:27.460
She fights She-Hulk.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.699
And then she also fights the Avengers and
The X-Men later.

00:04:29.699 --> 00:04:32.990
It feels like there's a lot of incongruous
match-ups happening.

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:33.990
Yeah.

00:04:33.990 --> 00:04:34.990
Okay.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:35.990
You got to let those heroes-

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.120
She fights a surprising amount of people.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:39.120
Ruby Thursday.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.120
Ruby Thursday.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.150
I think what it probably is, I think the reason
she fights a lot of people is because when

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:49.349
you start working at Marvel comics and you
go, "I need them to be able to beat someone

00:04:49.349 --> 00:04:53.260
really quickly in the first two pages of this
issue before we get to the real villain,"

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:58.210
they're like, "Oh yeah, Ruby Thursday, just
throw her in, getting arrested."

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.630
Like she's already been beaten for the reader
has shown up.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:06.539
She can be like Baron Zemo was for a while,
just floating around doing nefarious stuff

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.189
in a bunch of different movies.

00:05:08.189 --> 00:05:10.419
But rarely being the main antagonist.

00:05:10.419 --> 00:05:13.330
While also occasionally rearranging her face.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:14.330
Yeah.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:15.330
Right.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.022
That's hat on a hat, but I love it.

00:05:17.022 --> 00:05:21.009
I feel like Ruby Thursday is unlikely to make
an appearance.

00:05:21.009 --> 00:05:22.080
I agree, but a girl can dream.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.080
I'm glad I know about her, though.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.080
Yeah.

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.090
I just want everyone to know that she is she's
out there waiting.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.389
A strong female antagonist.

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:30.389
Yeah.

00:05:30.389 --> 00:05:32.860
Marvel, it's time.

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:33.860
Come on.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.860
You asked for weirdest.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.169
You asked me for weirdest, and I feel like
I really delivered here.

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:42.639
Not one person on this Zoom call is disappointed
in you right now, Nina, you're doing a terrific

00:05:42.639 --> 00:05:43.639
job.

00:05:43.639 --> 00:05:44.639
But okay.

00:05:44.639 --> 00:05:46.240
I have eight questions.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.240
Okay.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:52.039
Why is her name Ruby Thursday?

00:05:52.039 --> 00:05:56.880
It's a reference for the Rolling Stones song,
Ruby Tuesday.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:00.810
But I don't know why-

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.599
Keith Richards never sings...

00:06:02.599 --> 00:06:05.690
Hello, Ruby Thursday.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:06.690
That's the sequel.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:10.069
He was always lost in time and space, he can't
figure out what goes on face.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:11.069
No.

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:13.319
That's the only explanation that there is.

00:06:13.319 --> 00:06:17.750
She's just Ruby Thursday, and it's a Rolling
Stones reference, but they're never like,

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.529
"And here's the meaning behind it."

00:06:19.529 --> 00:06:21.529
She's a woman of mystery, Thomas.

00:06:22.819 --> 00:06:23.870
I guess.

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:28.879
Well, I'm in love with her.

00:06:28.879 --> 00:06:32.289
Tom, put your love away, just for a minute.

00:06:32.289 --> 00:06:36.439
I don't know if I have that in me, but I'm
going to give it the old college.

00:06:36.439 --> 00:06:42.210
Who are the weirdest villains or weirdest
characters, excuse me, that the MCU could

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.090
bring in in phase four?

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.530
So I feel like we've got all the classics,
the people that are just going to come up,

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:50.259
anytime that you Google "weirdest Marvel characters."

00:06:50.259 --> 00:06:55.550
You got your Great Lakes Avengers, you got
your, you get your Pet Avengers, you got those

00:06:55.550 --> 00:06:56.550
groups.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:03.720
I don't know, there's a lot of guys that haven't
gotten a lot of attention for good reason.

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:06.120
Slapstick was one of my favorites when I was
a kid.

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.120
Stupid character.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:08.120
I remember Slapstick.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:09.169
You remember Slapstick?

00:07:09.169 --> 00:07:11.349
I remember from the Marvel comics cards.

00:07:11.349 --> 00:07:13.259
I had the trading cards.

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:15.550
So I remember getting that card and saying,
"Slapstick."

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.499
"The hell is that?"

00:07:17.499 --> 00:07:18.499
Okay.

00:07:18.499 --> 00:07:21.779
And then like moving onto Nightcrawler, and
the heroes I liked.

00:07:21.779 --> 00:07:22.779
Right.

00:07:22.779 --> 00:07:23.779
Yeah.

00:07:23.779 --> 00:07:26.270
He was very much a lava glass Batman.

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:28.809
What does Slapstick do?

00:07:28.809 --> 00:07:30.550
The lava glass Batman.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.740
Yeah, of trading cards, he's the one that
you didn't really want, because

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.999
What does he do?

00:07:36.999 --> 00:07:40.909
He has all the powers, basically, of a Tex
Avery cartoon.

00:07:40.909 --> 00:07:46.219
He looks like a Chuck Jones character, he's
out there getting squashed by steamrollers

00:07:46.219 --> 00:07:47.849
and stuff.

00:07:47.849 --> 00:07:49.580
He pulls a giant mallet out of nowhere.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.110
He's a big old silly goof.

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:53.919
So, The Mask, starring Jim Carrey.

00:07:53.919 --> 00:07:55.330
You know what?

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:59.159
I would be a little bit flabbergasted if it
turned out that this character didn't pop

00:07:59.159 --> 00:08:01.319
up right after The Mask starring Jim Carrey.

00:08:01.319 --> 00:08:02.319
Yeah.

00:08:02.319 --> 00:08:03.319
Hmm.

00:08:03.319 --> 00:08:04.319
Yeah.

00:08:04.319 --> 00:08:05.319
Interesting.

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:06.319
That makes sense.

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:07.319
Yeah, but fun.

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:08.319
Who else?

00:08:08.319 --> 00:08:09.319
What'd we get?

00:08:09.319 --> 00:08:12.020
Like two-thirds of Alpha Flight I feel like
it would be very weird to see onscreen.

00:08:12.020 --> 00:08:13.119
Alpha Flight's pretty strange.

00:08:13.119 --> 00:08:14.119
Yeah.

00:08:14.119 --> 00:08:15.119
That's a good one.

00:08:15.119 --> 00:08:19.629
Alpha Flight is top-tier to me, but it is
inescapable that the vast majority of the

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:25.460
roster is made up of racial stereotypes, and
problematic archetypes.

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:27.779
Yeah, there's that.

00:08:27.779 --> 00:08:33.849
I think Puck spent the first five or six years
that he was a character just being funny because

00:08:33.849 --> 00:08:35.510
he's shorter than everybody.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:38.890
That was his entire defining character trait.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:39.890
Right.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:40.890
On behalf of short people everywhere.

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:41.890
That's insulting.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:47.279
And on behalf of the rest of us, look at you.

00:08:47.279 --> 00:08:49.389
You're doing a good job.

00:08:49.389 --> 00:08:50.389
All right.

00:08:50.389 --> 00:08:52.230
So let's see here.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:57.690
The version of Nixon that shot himself in
the Captain America comics back in the day,

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.230
I don't know if you guys remember that?

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:00.399
Oh yeah.

00:09:00.399 --> 00:09:06.110
They kept them really shadowing and stuff,
but he just full-on swallows a bullet right

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.389
there on the page.

00:09:07.389 --> 00:09:10.820
So that's one of your picks for weirdest characters
they can bring in?

00:09:10.820 --> 00:09:14.550
Yeah, that version of Nixon that shot himself
in the Captain America comic is my number

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.750
three pick.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.310
Actual Bucky from the comics, I feel like,
instead of like the re-imagined version the

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:25.339
one that is in arguably a 14-year-old with
a machine gun?

00:09:25.339 --> 00:09:28.190
I would love to see that onscreen.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:32.750
And then finally, Henry Cavill's Superman.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:34.600
That would be pretty weird.

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:36.940
Yeah, that would be weird.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:37.940
Yeah.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:38.940
What if?

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:41.950
Oh, but just to spring off of that, what if
they did Squadron Supreme?

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.589
What if they did?

00:09:43.589 --> 00:09:44.990
And cast Henry Cavill?

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:46.600
Cavill, excuse me.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.220
I don't know.

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.260
What's that dude's name?

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:51.009
Who's the leader of the Squadron Supreme?

00:09:51.009 --> 00:09:52.009
Oh, shoot.

00:09:52.009 --> 00:09:55.779
They're the JLA analogs in Marvel comics.

00:09:55.779 --> 00:09:57.860
It's not Century, is it?

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.389
Is it Hyperion?

00:09:59.389 --> 00:10:00.389
Maybe?

00:10:00.389 --> 00:10:01.389
That sounds right.

00:10:01.389 --> 00:10:02.470
I think Hyperion.

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:06.690
Let's just cut out this part where none of
us know anything.

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:07.690
Is it Hyperion?

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:08.690
It might be Hyperion.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:10.620
I think that's who it is in the Squadron Supreme.

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:14.389
I can't keep all of the dark re-imaginings
of Superman straight anymore.

00:10:14.389 --> 00:10:16.779
It's a little difficult.

00:10:16.779 --> 00:10:20.480
So my pick, I also thought of the Great Lakes
Avengers.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:24.100
I like Squirrel Girl a lot.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.100
Oh yeah.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.100
Squirrel Girl is a favorite.

00:10:26.100 --> 00:10:29.360
They were actually going to bring Squirrel
Girl into the MCU at some point.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:34.920
A few years ago, they announced a show that
they were going to put on TV that was going

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:38.050
to be part of the MCU with Milana Vayntrub
as Squirrel Girl.

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:39.050
That didn't happen.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:42.779
She does the voice in the cartoon.

00:10:42.779 --> 00:10:48.980
But my pick for the weirdest villain that
they could bring into the MCU, that I think

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:52.860
could actually show up in the MCU at some
point is Swarm.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:57.250
Are you familiar with Swarm?

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.250
I'm not.

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.370
Tom, are you familiar with Swarm?

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.170
I'm thinking of the thousand, I think.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:03.610
Who are you talking about?

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:07.160
Swarm is a Nazi scientist.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.199
Nope.

00:11:08.199 --> 00:11:17.760
Who is also a person-shaped swarm of bees
in a purple cape with white gloves.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:18.880
He wears a cape?

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:23.880
He wears a purple cape with a hood over his
mound-of-bees head.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:24.880
He has teeth.

00:11:24.880 --> 00:11:28.180
And he wears white gloves.

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.980
Yeah, I want to see this.

00:11:30.980 --> 00:11:32.779
And he's-

00:11:32.779 --> 00:11:34.290
Treacherously Todd McFarlane-y.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:36.220
Is this Todd McFarlane?

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:37.649
No, created by Bill Mantlo.

00:11:37.649 --> 00:11:38.649
I'll be damned.

00:11:38.649 --> 00:11:44.170
The creator of Rocket Raccoon, among many
other characters.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:50.470
He fought Champions, which was a bunch of
heroes out in LA that was comprised of-

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.009
Hercules-

00:11:52.009 --> 00:12:01.910
Hercules, Iceman, Ghost Rider, Angel, Black
Widow, and someone named Darkstar, who I'd

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:06.040
never heard of before, until I started looking
into Swarm's origins.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:07.040
I'm familiar, yeah.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:14.149
But Swarm is a former Nazi scientist who escaped
to, I want to say South America, Central America.

00:12:14.149 --> 00:12:16.860
And he was out there doing research on being
a Nazi.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.300
As one does.

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.230
And he's researching bees.

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:25.649
Well, he's like, "I need bees to take over
the world.

00:12:25.649 --> 00:12:27.160
Look at these bees."

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:32.769
And he says, "A comet hit the earth recently
and I think these bees were affected by that

00:12:32.769 --> 00:12:33.920
comet.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:38.690
If I can control these bees, I can take over
the world."

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:43.560
And so he builds a ray gun, shoots the bees,
and learns that he wasn't able to control

00:12:43.560 --> 00:12:46.459
the bees, but he was able to make them very
angry.

00:12:46.459 --> 00:12:48.009
So they swarm him-

00:12:48.009 --> 00:12:49.790
I am captivated right now.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:58.590
Sting him like crazy, and then his consciousness
is shredded, and is spread across the bees.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:02.800
And he is now a pile of bees shaped like a
guy.

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:10.459
And he fights The Champions, and they beat
him by Hercules throws the queen bee into

00:13:10.459 --> 00:13:12.089
the ocean.

00:13:12.089 --> 00:13:16.100
And so then all the bees leave, and then all
that's left is a pile of bones.

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:18.150
That sucks so hard.

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.779
I love it.

00:13:19.779 --> 00:13:21.970
He's come back since then, Swarm.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:27.329
Yeah, you don't just throw away a character
like Nazi scientist who gets stung by a bunch

00:13:27.329 --> 00:13:28.329
of bees.

00:13:28.329 --> 00:13:29.600
He's Nazi bees, Swarm.

00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:31.759
A bunch of Nazi bees.

00:13:31.759 --> 00:13:33.190
He's Nazi bees.

00:13:33.190 --> 00:13:34.190
I'm broken.

00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:35.860
You've broken me with this information.

00:13:35.860 --> 00:13:36.860
So there's Swarm.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:41.580
So that's who I think is the weirdest character
that they could bring into the MCU that I

00:13:41.580 --> 00:13:43.660
think would be great.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:45.100
Why not?

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:46.100
We've got-

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:53.360
Could you imagine being a racial superiority-based
villain and then going like, "You know what?

00:13:53.360 --> 00:13:58.720
It's probably fine if I'm a bunch of bees,
I got a lot of problems with different skin

00:13:58.720 --> 00:14:04.459
colors and lifestyles, but I think as long
as I'm white bees, I should be fine."

00:14:04.459 --> 00:14:06.300
Oh my god.

00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:08.139
So they're bees.

00:14:08.139 --> 00:14:09.370
He's bees.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.370
Swarm.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:11.370
He's bees.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.050
Oh my god.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:17.670
I want a Swarm movie, I want a Swarm franchise,
I want a Swarm action figure, I want Swarm

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:18.670
everything.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:20.430
You can buy a Swarm action figure.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:21.430
I was wondering.

00:14:21.430 --> 00:14:22.430
It exists.

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:28.930
I want to see 20,000 bees line up at a salon
